flowchart TB
    Problem["The RTGS liquidity problem:<br/>a bank must have the money at the<br/>instant it sends, but incoming payments<br/>do not arrive before outgoing ones"]

    Problem --> Options{"Options for the<br/>central bank"}

    Options -->|Refuse| Gridlock["Payments queue.<br/>Gridlock: everyone waits for<br/>everyone else to pay first"]
    Options -->|Lend intraday| Credit["Fed extends daylight credit<br/>against the master account"]

    Credit --> PSR["Payment System Risk policy<br/>governs how much and at what price"]

    PSR --> Cap["Net debit cap<br/>Multiple of risk-based capital"]
    PSR --> Price["Pricing"]
    PSR --> Weak["Institutions in weak condition:<br/>zero cap, prefunding required"]

    Cap --> C1["Exempt<br/>small, infrequent users"]
    Cap --> C2["De minimis<br/>board resolution"]
    Cap --> C3["Average / Above average / High<br/>board-approved self-assessment"]

    Price --> P1["Collateralized overdraft:<br/>zero fee since March 2011"]
    Price --> P2["Uncollateralized overdraft:<br/>50 basis points annual rate,<br/>prorated over the 22-hour day,<br/>with a per-period fee waiver"]

    P1 --> Effect["Effect: banks pledge collateral<br/>and borrow intraday for free.<br/>Unsecured central bank exposure<br/>is capped and priced."]
    P2 --> Effect

    Effect --> Result["Roughly 4 trillion USD a day clears<br/>on Fedwire without participants<br/>holding 4 trillion in reserves"]

    Gridlock -.the alternative CHIPS chose.-> Netting["Or: net the payments instead<br/>of funding them.<br/>See CHIPS."]

